    nuttx/spinlock.h: Disable up_testset if CONFIG_SPINLOCK=n

    The up_testset function is tied to the spinlock_t type, which defaults
    to empty if spinlocks are not used.

    If a generic up_testset is needed, the type must be strictly bound to
    the type EXPECTED by up_testset. Previously, sizeof(spinlock_t) was either
    the architecture specific word size (which is correct for up_testset) or
    1 byte (which is most definitely WRONG for up_testset).

    Fix the issue by disabling up_testset entirely.

    Signed-off-by: hujun5 <hujun5@xiaomi.com>

